sub1:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-douady-magnetic-drop-phyllotaxis> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-douady-magnetic-drop-phyllotaxis-overall> .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-douady-magnetic-drop-phyllotaxis-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Douady & Couder (1992, 1996) self-organized magnetic-drop phyllotaxis & imperfect pitchfork cascade — MorphoEval overall 90.2/100" ;
        dcterms:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dcterms:description "Pass 3 re-score of `1992-douady-magnetic-drop-phyllotaxis.py` (90.2/100, from 91.2 in Pass 2). The v3 script now lets the iterated placement map find the (1,1) -> (1,2) pitchfork by itself and measures the emergent threshold by bisection (G_c1^emp = 0.8595 vs the analytic full-chain root 0.859019, |error| 4.5e-4, within the finite-iteration bias), uses the dynamical discriminant S_dyn(G) instead of a hard-coded 0.85901889 in the equilibrium diagram, triangulates the true radii r_k = exp(kG) with Douady & Couder's nearest-neighbour contact definition (9/10 Fibonacci table rows, (2,3) at G = 0.30 where the v2 clipped geometry gave (3,5), Lucas (3,4) at G = 0.11 and (4,7) at G = 0.06), displays Row B and the GIF in the dish geometry rho = 1 + kG so the parastichy lattices are visible, adds an N_mem sweep (converged within 0.5 deg at N_mem = 8) and a comparison with the six tabulated dish regimes (RMSE 0.141 deg, 6/6 pairs), and inverts the specimen's own (5,8) reciprocal-lattice peaks to alpha_emp = 138.03 deg (inside the Lean 4 Theorem 5 window 135-138.46 deg, 0.52 deg from the golden angle) and G_emp = 0.0308, with the inversion validated on the simulated lattice. Two Lean 4 theorems were added (5 total, 0 sorrys). The score falls slightly because the re-read exposed that v2's thresholds were imposed, its Delaunay pairs mislabelled at transitions, its N = 123 'scales' were detections, and the vendored reference JSON mislabels G_fold as G_c1 and carries dish-regime divergence values of unquantified provenance; those are disclosed here rather than credited. Overall 90.2/100 (faithfulness 89.8, reproducibility 91.1); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit d58a084; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 92, Morphological realism / specimen match 88, Parameter expressivity 91, Morphometric validation 89, Source and data traceability 90, Code-to-model traceability 91, Reproducibility package 92. Output judged: docs/media/magnetic_drop_phyllotaxis_comparison.png: rendered output of 1992-douady-magnetic-drop-phyllotaxis.py at d58a084, image/png, 1780387 B, 2590×2408 px, artifact_sha256 09cbec33b6c20133934e29b9b7d5f3a8061d3f6cb4e1ddb93832f9db58f2db6d (sha256 09cbec33b6c20133934e29b9b7d5f3a8061d3f6cb4e1ddb93832f9db58f2db6d), spec_fingerprint 045b0921b1b4726ce33d0ec3190a3812d349153acf150593c5bf6c01da8f1e43. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 045b0921b1b4726ce33d0ec3190a3812d349153acf150593c5bf6c01da8f1e43; artifact_sha256: 09cbec33b6c20133934e29b9b7d5f3a8061d3f6cb4e1ddb93832f9db58f2db6d; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/magnetic_drop_phyllotaxis/conifer_cone_specimen.jpg=7bcb68e856d4db53..., datasets/magnetic_drop_phyllotaxis/magnetic_drop_phyllotaxis_reference.json=9ae33106a0fea23f..., datasets/magnetic_drop_phyllotaxis/paper_citations.bib=2c3aa1ec0e4c53de...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-19-magnetic-drop-phyllotaxis-audit-v2. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Douady & Couder (1992) Phys. Rev. Lett. 68:2098-2101 iterative magnetic-dipole repulsion energy E(phi) = sum_{k>=1} d_k(phi, phi_{n-k})^{-3} on a circular rim r = R_0 with linear dish advection r_k = R_0(1 + kG) controlled by the plastochron ratio G = V T / R_0; Figs. 1-2 dish regimes (1,1), (2,3), (3,5), (5,8), (8,13) and a metastable Lucas (4,7) | Douady & Couder (1992) Fig. 3 & (1996) J. Theor. Biol. 178:255-274 Secs. 3-4: supercritical (1,1)->(1,2) pitchfork of the iterated map, imperfect pitchfork cascade along the Fibonacci branch -> 137.508 deg, disconnected Lucas branch -> 99.502 deg, and nearest-neighbour contact parastichies on the van Iterson lattice; reconstructed_in_script: Exact static Hessian fold (G_fold = 0.773484 exp / 2.514560 lin) AND dynamical pitchfork (G_c1 = 0.859019 exp full chain / 3.631432 lin 2-drop) roots, the EMERGENT threshold of the unclamped iterated map (G_c1^emp = 0.8595 by bisection), the regular-spiral zero-force locus F(G, dphi) = 0, and adiabatic continuation along both Fibonacci (r = 0.99999, RMSE = 0.065 deg, contact pairs 9/10 table rows) and Lucas (RMSE = 0.141 deg) branches | Nearest-neighbour contact parastichy pairs on the true radii r_k = exp(kG) (Delaunay census kept as a secondary, biased extractor), memory-depth sweep N_mem in {1,2,3,5,8,13,21,45}, gamma in {1,3,5} universality, and simulated divergence / pair at the six tabulated dish regimes (RMSE 0.141 deg, 6/6 pairs) | Reciprocal-lattice inversion m*alpha + omega_m*G = 2*pi*j_m of the sub-bin (5, 8) log-polar FFT peaks of `conifer_cone_specimen.jpg` giving alpha_emp = 138.03 deg and G_emp = 0.0308, validated on a synthetic log-polar image of the simulated G = 0.06 lattice (0.014 deg / 0.06 % recovery error); transfer_boundary: Exponential meristem advection r_k = R_0 exp(kG) is displayed in the log-radial projection rho = 1 + ln(r/R_0) = 1 + kG, which coincides with the PRL 1992 silicone-oil dish geometry; the mature cone's apparent radial law fits the linear dish law better (R^2 0.977) than the exponential law (R^2 0.899), and its lattice is not perfectly log-periodic (closure residual 2.2 bins), so G_emp = 0.031 is an effective, not a developmental, plastochron ratio | The 'observed' per-regime divergence means in the reference table are regime-level readings of Douady & Couder (1992) Figs. 1-2 and text, not digitised data with uncertainties; the dish-regime RMSE of 0.141 deg should be read against that provenance; does_not_claim: Subcellular PIN1 polar auxin efflux carrier trafficking or continuous reaction-diffusion PDE dynamics on the meristem (Slot 033 Jönsson et al. 2006 / Smith et al. 2006); 3D photogrammetric or micro-CT cone reconstruction (the specimen analysis is a single 2D apical photograph of a 3D cone); a scale-level segmentation of the cone (the DoG detections over-count by ~2x and are not used at lattice level)." ;
        dcterms:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: 1992-douady-magnetic-drop-phyllotaxis.py:1113-1130 — the mature cone's radial law fits linear advection (R^2 0.977) better than exponential (0.899); implement the linear-lattice (Archimedean) variant of the reciprocal-lattice inversion, or invert in (r, theta) rather than (ln r, theta), and report the specimen's G under both laws with the closure residual as a model-selection statistic.",
            "remediation needed: 1992-douady-magnetic-drop-phyllotaxis.py:1369-1380 and 1491-1510 — the specimen comparison is in log-polar and (G, alpha) space; overlay the inverted (alpha_emp = 138.03 deg, G_emp = 0.031, chirality -1) lattice as a synthetic point set on the photograph in Panel C1 (and a photo-coordinate rendering of the simulated (5,8) lattice beside it), and replace the DoG detections by a lattice-guided scale segmentation so the detection count equals the scale count.",
            "remediation needed: 1992-douady-magnetic-drop-phyllotaxis.py:446-476 — compute_equilibrium_bifurcation_diagram labels the spiral branches stable/unstable by the sign of the static Hessian S(G, dphi) while the 180-deg branch now uses the dynamical discriminant S_dyn(G); implement the linearised multiplier of the iterated map about a regular spiral (Jacobian of phi_n = argmin E w.r.t. the k preceding angles) so every branch of Panel A1 carries the same dynamical stability criterion, and add a Lean 4 integer witness for the (1,2)->(2,3) transition.",
            "remediation needed: 1992-douady-magnetic-drop-phyllotaxis.py:610-620 and 347-398 — the memory depth N_mem = 45 is an ad-hoc truncation; replace it by the physical dish exit (drops leave at R_max/R_0 = 8, i.e. k_exit = 7/G for linear advection, as in `ferrofluid_experiment_parameters`) and extrapolate the emergent threshold in 1/n_iter to remove the +4.5e-4 finite-iteration bias instead of tolerating it.",
            "remediation needed: 1992-douady-magnetic-drop-phyllotaxis.py:797-814 — the gamma universality sweep is evaluated only at G = 0.06; sweep gamma in {1,3,5} across the full cascade (and across the linear dish law up to its own G_c1 = 3.63) so the universality claim and the dish model's cascade are tested, not asserted.",
            "remediation needed: datasets/magnetic_drop_phyllotaxis/magnetic_drop_phyllotaxis_reference.json:65-86 and 109-125 — re-pin the table (update EXPECTED_SHA256 at 1992-douady-magnetic-drop-phyllotaxis.py:123-134) with the keys renamed static_fold_* / dynamical_pitchfork_* , the G = 0.35 row's pair corrected to (1,2) or marked transitional, detected_scale_umbos_count replaced by detections + FFT-consistent scale count, and the dish-regime divergence means replaced by digitised Fig. 3 points with reading uncertainties; add van Iterson (1907) to paper_citations.bib and re-pin it." ;
        pk:hasScore "0.902"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Gemini 4 Argon (primary) + Claude Sonnet 5.5 High (independent second assessor)" ;
        dcterms:identifier "gemini-4-argon" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf orcid:0009-0007-4948-9192 ;
        foaf:homepage <https://deepmind.google> .
}

